<div class="custom-important">
  <span class="alert-icon"></span>
  <strong>Rigor</strong><br><br>
  LLMs are double-edged with respect to rigor. On the one hand, wielded carefully, they can help us sharpen our own thinking by pointing out holes in our own reasoning or otherwise providing thought-provoking suggestions. On the other, if used recklessly or thoughtlessly, they can have the opposite effect, replacing crisp thinking with generated flotsam. LLMs are useful in as much as they promote and reinforce our rigor.

